      "body": "## Overview\n\nSkip the DeepEP low-latency tests on B200 until the NVSHMEM bug in pytorch/test-infra#9101 is fixed. Both B200 jobs are `optional: true`.\n\n## Claims\n\n- `config-b200.txt`: the four `deepep-ll` entries are commented out.\n- The B200 EPLB job runs only `deepep_high_throughput` (`SKIP_DEEPEP_LL=1`).\n- Other entries, H100 and ROCm are unchanged, and the rest of each shard still runs.\n\n## Validation\n\n- On `main` over 60 days, these two jobs failed in 76 of 364 runs (about 21%; 4.5% to 42% by week, 11.5% and 4.5% in the last two). Of the 24 most recent failures, 19 show the NVSHMEM chain `ibv_modify_qp failed` → `ep_connect failed` → `nvshmem setup connections failed`, and each costs about 50 minutes. Examples: [daily 96139](https://buildkite.com/vllm/ci/builds/96139), [nightly 95338](https://buildkite.com/vllm/ci/builds/95338). Build 96292 (#55387) hit it in all three jobs, and retries passed.\n- `config-b200.txt` parses to 9 configs with no `deepep-ll`. The EPLB backend choice was checked with and without the flag, and `shellcheck` is clean. The Buildkite jobs were not run.\n\n## Details\n\nCause: an NVSHMEM bootstrap bug, probably fixed in 3.8.0, not a torch issue. This drops the B200 low-latency signal while it is in place; other tests in a failing shard still ran and passed in 96292. Alternatives: test NVSHMEM 3.8.0, or add an automatic retry.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [ ] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n",
